                        "content": "The nurse is caring for the client who is suspected of having lung cancer. The nurse would assess the client for which most frequent early symptom of lung cancer?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "11797937e327eb6d913faa80427c566b",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Analyzing 分析",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nCough is the most frequent early symptom of lung cancer, which begins as nonproductive and hacking and progresses to productive. In the smoker who already has a cough, a change in the character and frequency of cough usually occurs. Hoarseness indicates that the affected tissue is in the upper airway. Wheezing and blood-streaked sputum (hemoptysis) are later signs of lung cancer. Pain is a very late sign and is usually pleuritic in nature.",
                        "id": "1ccd70dfa2d0434489c4f0bedf3beb56",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "c927870cd2c34584852c161761e42a61",
                                "content": "Avoid driving the car for a few days."
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "d0c80632be0d4770aefdd6a36caa9c7b",
                                "content": "Restrict fluid intake to prevent incontinence."
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "1",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "993434d2c3284ea98a1f65199d808ddb",
                                "content": "Avoid lifting objects heavier than 20 lb (9 kg) for at least 6 weeks."
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "3a84a3db08b8442a97bbe8d263c89ea4",
                                "content": "Notify the primary health care provider if small blood clots are noticed during urination."
                            }
