                        "content": "The nurse caring for a client with lung cancer assesses for which early sign of vena cava syndrome?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "11797937e327eb6d913faa80427c566b",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Analyzing 分析",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nVena cava syndrome occurs when the superior vena cava is compressed or obstructed by tumor growth. Early signs and symptoms generally occur in the morning and include edema of the face, especially around the eyes, and client complaints of tightness of a shirt or blouse collar. As the compression worsens, the client experiences edema of the hands and arms. Mental status changes and cyanosis are late signs.\n",
                        "id": "4aa1148e776d4f64b8d7c696a78b115d",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "143f88fe92bc46019d4d325f9cf1a4d5",
                                "content": "Thyroid cancer"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "c6c54e7331854809a16c2a60e9445323",
                                "content": "Acute laryngitis"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "1",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "7f826792ae944feb86e31dfae4f2029a",
                                "content": "Laryngeal cancer"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "d6fce2a5d260407e90e0f60a6e2eb452",
                                "content": "Bronchogenic cancer"
                            }
                        ],
                        "extJson": {
                            "optionList": [
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "143f88fe92bc46019d4d325f9cf1a4d5",
                                    "content": "Thyroid cancer"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "c6c54e7331854809a16c2a60e9445323",
                                    "content": "Acute laryngitis"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "1",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "7f826792ae944feb86e31dfae4f2029a",
                                    "content": "Laryngeal cancer"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "d6fce2a5d260407e90e0f60a6e2eb452",
